dd deposit and withdraw commands with core structure","messageBody":"Implement deposit (#8) and withdraw (#9). These are the first features that create transactions, so add the shared base they need: Transaction, TransactionList, Command, Parser, Ui and FinNusException. Other commands (balance, recent, delete, help) can be added as new Command subclasses. Parser accepts parameters in any order, rejects invalid amounts (negative, zero, more than 2 decimals, NaN, scientific notation) and requires a description for withdraw. Add JUnit tests for parsing, commands and Transaction formatting.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":416,"deletions":11},"test-code":{"insertions":172,"deletions":12}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"8dd358993af96157db0ee932df21319daa5e7b3d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use BigDecimal for amounts and add no-description deposit constructor","messageBody":"double cannot represent most decimal values exactly (e.g. 0.1 + 0.2 \u003d 0.30000000000000004), so balances would drift and comparisons could be wrong. BigDecimal keeps amounts exact. Add DepositCommand(BigDecimal) for deposits without a description, as suggested in review. Enable assertions for the Gradle run task.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":39,"deletions":18},"other":{"insertions":2,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":37,"deletions":12}}}]}],"chancheese":[{"date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"b7b6780967ec5a849fc42ece7762fc6f2923eac9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add my own About Us","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"59962eb92fb46d567e2d39c867ef13c58f55f218","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into chancheese-AboutUs","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"8f39b1fe8af8c9f175762e594105598956972bb6","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull r